WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.600
that gives us a longitudinal data set that can really help us interpret the impact we're

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.580
seeing. And I think most important for us is the muscle manifestations. I know there's been a lot

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.280
of discussion as well about CNS, but I think in this particular disease,

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:16.940
what we're seeing is a lot of muscle manifestations. And I think that's a lot of

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:23.200
really matters is muscle mobility and managing those muscle-related manifestations. And that's

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:29.980
very much our focus. So having, I think, 54-week follow-up long-term data on a large cohort of

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.420
patients gives you a very robust read. And I think we feel confident that based on everything

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.840
we've seen in the phase two study, that we're set up well, as well as we can be towards that

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:48.140
phase three readout. Next question. Thank you. Your next question comes from the

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:52.220
line of Florent Cespedes from OdoBHF. Please go ahead.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:58.060
Good afternoon. Thank you very much for taking my questions. Florent Cespedes from OdoBHF.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:05.900
A big picture question for Vas. On your last slide, you highlighted that

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:11.580
there will be multiple readouts in H2 that could raise your mid-term to long-term growth outlook.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:17.900
Maybe, Vas, could you be a little bit more specific and give us a bit more color or from where do you see that?

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:21.020
Do you see the potential upside coming from? Thank you.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:28.380
Yeah, thanks, Florent. When you look at what we guided to last fall, our focus was very much

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:36.700
on what we had in hand and a probabilized view of our pipeline. And I think when then some of

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.060
these medicines, as they ultimately come forward and we unprobabilize, that can lead to significant

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:47.900
upsides versus where we are today. I think, obviously, the big readouts, not surprisingly,

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:55.260
I think to all of you, will certainly be Remibrutinib for the 5-year term. Remibrutinib in MS.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:02:03.180
Remibrutinib in HS. Deldisran in DM1. We also believe, you know, Yinalumab and Firstline ITB

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:09.340
can be a billion-dollar-plus indication. I think Palacarcin will be significant. I think it will

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:16.260
take longer to build over time. And I think, overall, the combination of Palacarcin plus DIY235 will give us a very significant improvement.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:16.760
Thank you.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:17.260
Thank you.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.420
again, opportunity. But in that kind of five-year term, I think that medicine will take time

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:27.460
to build up. But, you know, I think those are the medicines where, you know, if we see some wins,

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:33.920
it could allow us to, once we do the modeling, to reevaluate the 5% to 6% growth up to 2030

